# Active Call State & OS Awareness

## How the OS knows about a call

| Runtime | Mechanism | What the OS shows |
|---------|-----------|-------------------|
| **All browsers** | `navigator.mediaSession` | macOS Now Playing widget, Windows media overlay, Android media notification |
| **All browsers** | Screen Wake Lock API | Prevents screen from dimming/sleeping |
| **All browsers** | `document.title` | Tab shows `🔴 02:15 — standup` with timer |
| **Electron (macOS)** | `powerSaveBlocker` | Prevents system sleep |
| **Electron (macOS)** | `app.dock.setBadge("📞")` | Phone icon on dock badge |
| **Electron (all)** | Tray tooltip | `Workspace — In call: standup (5 participants)` |
| **Electron (all)** | IPC channels | Main process manages power + tray |
| **All** | `beforeunload` | Call ended on page close (best-effort) |

## Module

`shared/lib/call-state.ts` — unified call state manager.

```ts
import { callState, useCallState } from "~/shared/lib/call-state";

// Start a call (triggers all OS integrations)
callState.start({ roomName: "standup", participants: 3 });

// Update during call
callState.updateParticipants(5);
callState.setMuted(true);
callState.setVideoOn(false);

// End the call (releases all resources)
callState.end();

// Query
callState.getStatus();      // "idle" | "connecting" | "active"
callState.getActiveCall();   // { roomName, startedAt, participants, muted, videoOn } | null
callState.getCallDuration(); // seconds since start

// React hook
const { status, call, duration } = useCallState();
```

## Integration with JitsiCallModal

```tsx
// In jitsi-call.ui.tsx — when call opens:
useEffect(() => {
  if (open && parsed) {
    callState.start({ roomName: parsed.roomName });
  }
  return () => {
    callState.end();
  };
}, [open, parsed?.roomName]);

// When participant count updates:
useEffect(() => {
  if (participantCount != null) {
    callState.updateParticipants(participantCount);
  }
}, [participantCount]);
```

## Electron IPC

Renderer → Main process channels:

| Channel | Payload | Main process action |
|---------|---------|---------------------|
| `call:start` | `{ room, participants }` | Start `powerSaveBlocker`, update tray tooltip, set dock badge |
| `call:end` | — | Stop `powerSaveBlocker`, restore tray tooltip, restore dock badge |
| `call:update` | `{ participants }` | Update tray tooltip |

## Media Session API

When a call is active, `navigator.mediaSession` shows:
- **Title**: `Call: {roomName}`
- **Artist**: `{N} participants`
- **Album**: `Workspace`

Action handlers:
- **Pause** → mute the call
- **Play** → unmute
- **Stop** → end the call

This appears in macOS Now Playing, Windows system media transport controls, and Chrome's media hub.

## Screen Wake Lock

Automatically acquired on call start, released on call end.
If the lock is released (e.g., tab hidden), it's re-acquired when the tab becomes visible again.

## Rules for AI Agent

### When implementing call features

1. **Always call `callState.start()`** when a call begins — not just when the UI opens
2. **Always call `callState.end()`** in cleanup — useEffect return, modal close, page unload
3. **Update participants** via `callState.updateParticipants()` when count changes
4. **Never manage wake lock manually** — `call-state.ts` handles it
5. **Never modify document.title during a call** — `call-state.ts` manages the title pulse

### Do NOT

- Do NOT create a separate `powerSaveBlocker` — it's managed by the call state
- Do NOT forget to call `end()` — leaked calls prevent system sleep permanently
- Do NOT access `navigator.mediaSession` directly — go through `callState`
